---
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import ProductSubNav from "../../components/ProductSubNav.astro";
import TerminalWindow from "../../components/TerminalWindow.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import { WEB_ROUTES, DOCS_ROUTES, docsUrl } from "@niki/theme/site";
---

<PageHeader
  eyebrow="Product · Security"
  title="Hermetic by default."
  description="Agents execute inside rootless containers with dropped capabilities, a read-only root filesystem, and blocked network egress. Your working tree is never touched mid-run. Fail-closed posture when you can't be there to answer."
  canonicalPath="/product/security"
>
  <div class="nk-pagehead__actions" slot="actions">
    <a class="nk-btn nk-btn--primary" href={docsUrl(DOCS_ROUTES.security)}>Security docs</a>
  </div>
</PageHeader>

<ProductSubNav />

<section class="nk-section nk-container" aria-labelledby="sandbox-heading">
  <div class="nk-section-head">
    <p class="nk-eyebrow">Sandboxing</p>
    <h2 id="sandbox-heading">A container per run. A copy of your repo.</h2>
    <p>
      Niki binds your project into the sandbox as a copy — the pipeline never mutates your working
      tree mid-run. Three backends cover every trust level:
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="nk-grid nk-grid--3">
    <article class="nk-card">
      <h3>Podman (default)</h3>
      <p>Rootless, no daemon. Recommended — the least-privilege default path.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="nk-card">
      <h3>Docker</h3>
      <p>Same hardening when Podman isn't available. Identical image, identical policy.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="nk-card">
      <h3>Git worktree</h3>
      <p>
        No container runtime at all — an isolated git worktree plus local process. Prints a
        host-privilege warning so you know what you opted into.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div class="nk-sec-grid">
    <CodeBlock
      label="sandbox hardening — niki.toml"
      lang="toml"
      code={`[sandbox]
backend   = "podman"          # or "docker", "worktree"
image     = "niki-sandbox:24.04"
cap_drop  = "ALL"             # drop every Linux capability
rootfs    = "read-only"       # read-only root filesystem

[general]
network_disabled = true       # egress blocked unless allowlisted`}
    />
    <div class="nk-sec-list">
      <h3>Layered controls</h3>
      <ul class="nk-checklist">
        <li><code class="nk-inline">CapDrop ALL</code> — every Linux capability dropped</li>
        <li>Read-only root filesystem; workspace is the only writable bind mount</li>
        <li>
          Command deny-lists — <code class="nk-inline">rm -rf /</code>, <code class="nk-inline"
            >curl | sh</code
          > blocked by policy
        </li>
        <li>
          Hermeticity violations abort the run (<code class="nk-inline">HermeticityViolation</code>)
        </li>
        <li>
          Secrets redacted from logs and reports — including <code class="nk-inline">?key=</code> query
          params
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="nk-section nk-container" aria-labelledby="permissions-heading">
  <div class="nk-section-head">
    <p class="nk-eyebrow">Permissions</p>
    <h2 id="permissions-heading">Fail-closed when unattended.</h2>
    <p>
      The ask tool never invents answers; the approval tool denies by default when no human can
      respond. Permission modes scope what agents may do without you:
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="nk-grid nk-grid--4">
    <article class="nk-card">
      <span class="nk-mono nk-card__mode">manual</span>
      <p>Ask before anything consequential. The interactive default posture.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="nk-card">
      <span class="nk-mono nk-card__mode">auto</span>
      <p>Run the pipeline with in-policy actions allowed, per your config.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="nk-card">
      <span class="nk-mono nk-card__mode">dontask</span>
      <p>Headless: no prompts, deny on ambiguity, record everything.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="nk-card">
      <span class="nk-mono nk-card__mode">bypass</span>
      <p>Explicit, loud, for trusted sandboxes you control. Never silent.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <ul class="nk-checklist nk-sec-extra">
    <li>
      <code class="nk-inline">--permission-mode</code> flag and <code class="nk-inline"
        >[permissions] mode</code
      > config
    </li>
    <li>
      <code class="nk-inline">disable_worktree</code> kill-switch for the no-container backend
    </li>
    <li>
      <code class="nk-inline">fail_closed_headless</code> — unanswerable approvals fail the run, not silently
      pass
    </li>
    <li>
      Lifecycle hooks (<code class="nk-inline">[hooks.commands]</code>) can block runs fail-closed
      at each stage boundary
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="nk-section nk-container" aria-labelledby="spend-heading">
  <div class="nk-split">
    <div>
      <p class="nk-eyebrow">Cost control</p>
      <h2 id="spend-heading">A spend cap that actually stops.</h2>
      <p>
        Niki meters every agent call — tokens split into cached-input, reasoning and output — and
        enforces <code class="nk-inline">spend_cap_usd</code> hard: the run aborts before a branch is
        created if the estimate exceeds your ceiling. Unpriced models warn loudly instead of silently
        costing <code class="nk-inline">$0.00</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="nk-after">
        <a class="nk-link-arrow" href={WEB_ROUTES.pricing}>What a task costs</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <TerminalWindow title="cost report">
      <span class="nk-t-line nk-t-brand">$ niki report 6d281d6d</span>
      <span class="nk-t-line nk-t-dim">…</span>
      <span class="nk-t-line"
        ><span class="nk-t-m">tokens&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>in 2,912 · cached 1,204 · out 251</span
      >
      <span class="nk-t-line"
        ><span class="nk-t-m">cost&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>est. <span class="nk-t-ok"
          >$0.0112</span
        > (claude-sonnet-4 meter rates)</span
      >
      <span class="nk-t-line"
        ><span class="nk-t-m">cap&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>$5.00 · <span
          class="nk-t-ok">not exceeded</span
        ></span
      >
      <span class="nk-t-line"
        ><span class="nk-t-m">trace&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>trace.jsonl · OTLP export
        available</span
      >
    </TerminalWindow>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="nk-section nk-container" aria-labelledby="audit-heading">
  <div class="nk-section-head">
    <p class="nk-eyebrow">Auditability</p>
    <h2 id="audit-heading">The whole decision trail, on disk.</h2>
    <p>Every run writes artifacts you can inspect, diff, replay and hand to an auditor:</p>
  </div>
  <div class="nk-audit-grid">
    <div class="nk-audit-item">
      <span class="nk-mono">report.md</span>
      <p>Human-readable run report — verdict, scores, revisions, costs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-audit-item">
      <span class="nk-mono">changes.patch</span>
      <p>The unified diff — reviewable with anything that reads patches.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-audit-item">
      <span class="nk-mono">artifacts/*.json</span>
      <p>Per-agent JSON artifacts, schema-validated — what each agent decided and why.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-audit-item">
      <span class="nk-mono">safety_proof.json</span>
      <p>Sandbox and policy proofs for the run.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-audit-item">
      <span class="nk-mono">trace.jsonl</span>
      <p>Per-span event trace — an honestly derived timeline of the pipeline.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-audit-item">
      <span class="nk-mono">niki audit</span>
      <p>Consolidated JSON compliance bundle for one task: record, proofs, costs, trace.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="nk-section nk-container" aria-labelledby="privacy-heading">
  <div class="nk-oss">
    <div>
      <p class="nk-eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h2 id="privacy-heading">No telemetry. Ever.</h2>
      <p>
        The only outbound traffic Niki makes is your LLM provider API calls — or none at all with a
        local Ollama. No analytics, no phone-home, no hosted service. Keys are redacted from logs
        and reports by design.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="nk-oss__actions">
      <a class="nk-btn nk-btn--secondary" href={docsUrl(DOCS_ROUTES.security)}>Full security docs</a
      >
      <a
        class="nk-btn nk-btn--secondary"
        href={docsUrl("/sandboxing-security/enterprise-readiness")}
      >
        Enterprise readiness
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .nk-sec-grid {
    margin-top: var(--nk-space-4);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--nk-space-3);
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .nk-sec-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--nk-space-6);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .nk-sec-list h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-sec-extra {
    margin-top: var(--nk-space-4);
  }

  .nk-card__mode {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--nk-magenta);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--nk-magenta) 35%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--nk-magenta) 8%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--nk-radius-pill);
    padding: 2px 12px;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--nk-space-1);
  }

  .nk-split {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--nk-space-4);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .nk-split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--nk-space-6);
    }
  }

  .nk-split h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-split > div > p {
    margin-top: var(--nk-space-2);
  }

  .nk-audit-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--nk-space-2);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .nk-audit-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .nk-audit-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .nk-audit-item {
    border: 1px solid var(--nk-surface-border);
    border-radius: var(--nk-radius-card);
    padding: var(--nk-space-2);
    background: var(--nk-bg-1);
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .nk-audit-item > span {
    color: var(--nk-mint);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .nk-audit-item p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--nk-text-muted);
  }

  .nk-oss {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--nk-space-3);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .nk-oss {
      grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--nk-space-6);
    }
  }

  .nk-oss__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--nk-space-1);
  }
</style>
